# Built output — bytes must survive the round trip through git unchanged.
#
# rules.json is the reason this file exists. The site publishes its SHA-256 and
# invites the reader to recompute it with:
#
#     curl -s https://hh0hh.com/rules.json | sha256sum
#
# On Windows, core.autocrlf=true would rewrite LF to CRLF on checkout, changing
# every byte of every line and therefore the digest — turning a verifiable
# claim into a wrong one, silently, with no failing build anywhere.
* -text
